WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:06.160
Game of Thrones Season 8 Episode 1 is called
Winterfell – and it sets up the conflicts

00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:08.760
and mysteries for the final season.

00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:11.540
The Thrones title sequence has had an update.

00:00:11.540 --> 00:00:16.769
This astrolabe thingy used to show old historical
events – the Doom of Valyria, and Robert’s

00:00:16.769 --> 00:00:17.769
Rebellion.

00:00:17.769 --> 00:00:19.919
But now it shows recent events.

00:00:19.919 --> 00:00:23.820
This shot shows the dragon Viserion breaking
the Wall last season.

00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:28.339
You can see the army of the dead watching,
and Bran’s ravens overhead.

00:00:28.339 --> 00:00:30.249
This next scene shows the Red Wedding.

00:00:30.249 --> 00:00:34.720
The direwolf head is for Robb Stark, killed
by the flayed man of Bolton.

00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:39.460
There’s also the Lannister lion, Tully fish,
and Frey castle.

00:00:39.460 --> 00:00:43.610
This last shot shows a comet and a dragon
with three smaller dragons.

00:00:43.610 --> 00:00:49.150
That’s Daenerys Targaryen hatching her three
dragons in Season 1, beneath the red comet.

00:00:49.150 --> 00:00:54.920
So together, these opening shots sum up the
last seven seasons of Thrones – in ice and

00:00:54.920 --> 00:00:56.800
blood and fire.

00:00:56.800 --> 00:00:59.450
It gives a sense that history is happening.

00:00:59.450 --> 00:01:03.760
These wars with Daenerys and Starks and white
walkers – the maesters’ll write books

00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:08.479
about them one day – if anyone survives
the walkers.

00:01:08.479 --> 00:01:13.789
The episode’s set in three places – Winterfell,
King’s Landing, and Last Hearth.

00:01:13.789 --> 00:01:19.170
King Jon and Queen Daenerys arrive at Winterfell
– just like Season 1 Episode 1 had King

00:01:19.170 --> 00:01:21.840
Robert and Queen Cersei coming to Winterfell.

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:27.240
A young boy climbs up to get a good view,
just like Bran and Arya did in Season 1 – so

00:01:27.240 --> 00:01:30.429
there are lots of callbacks this episode.

00:01:30.429 --> 00:01:34.760
Tyrion and Varys talk about balls – there’s
been a lot of talk of balls and butts and

00:01:34.760 --> 00:01:38.110
dicks ever since the tv show ran out of books
to adapt.

00:01:38.110 --> 00:01:42.890
Season 8 is all new material, so not even
the book nerds know what’s coming.

00:01:42.890 --> 00:01:47.569
The people of the north look on Daenerys with
suspicion . Some see her as an invader, with

00:01:47.569 --> 00:01:53.399
a foreign army of eunuchs and “savages”
– Grey Worm and Missandei feel a long way

00:01:53.399 --> 00:01:54.819
from home.

00:01:54.819 --> 00:02:00.270
The northmen also remember Daenerys’ father
the Mad King, who killed the old Starks twenty

00:02:00.270 --> 00:02:01.270
years ago.

00:02:01.270 --> 00:02:03.729
So Daenerys needs to prove herself to the
north.

00:02:03.729 --> 00:02:09.220
Her dragons fly overhead, terrifying the northerners,
and Daenerys looks smug.

00:02:09.220 --> 00:02:14.650
Like Tyrion once said, Daenerys needs to scare
people a bit to be taken seriously as a ruler.

00:02:14.650 --> 00:02:20.440
But if she relies totally on fear, she’s
no better than her tyrannical father . Jon

00:02:20.440 --> 00:02:26.220
warmly reunites with Bran, he says Bran’s
a man now, like he’s all grown up, and Bran

00:02:26.220 --> 00:02:31.500
says “Almost” . Because Bran isn’t quite
Bran any more, he’s become the three-eyed

00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:36.600
raven, a magical consciousness of the old
gods that gives him visions and powers – and

00:02:36.600 --> 00:02:43.580
the raven is not “entirely human” . Bran
acts weird this episode, with lots of ominous

00:02:43.580 --> 00:02:44.580
stares.

00:02:44.580 --> 00:02:48.730
It may be that because of Bran’s visions,
he knows everything that’s gonna happen,

00:02:48.730 --> 00:02:54.300
and he’s guiding everyone along a pre-destined
path, even though he knows there’s tragedy

00:02:54.300 --> 00:02:55.480
along the way.

00:02:55.480 --> 00:02:58.790
That’s kinda what the original three-eyed
raven did.

00:02:58.790 --> 00:03:03.540
In the books, he’s called Bloodraven, and
he does terrible things for the sake of prophecy

00:03:03.540 --> 00:03:05.950
and the greater good – go watch that video.

00:03:05.950 --> 00:03:11.430
So the point is that Bran’s magic is powerful,
but it comes at a cost.

00:03:11.430 --> 00:03:16.400
There’s a big meeting, and there’s tension
between Jon Sansa and Daenerys – cause it’s

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:21.270
not clear who’s in charge . Sansa is the
Lady of Winterfell – she’s been here running

00:03:21.270 --> 00:03:24.990
things while Jon was off fighting zombies
and rooting his aunt.

00:03:24.990 --> 00:03:29.610
Jon is King in the North, but he gave up his
crown by kneeling to Daenerys.

00:03:29.610 --> 00:03:34.310
The northern lords chose Jon because they
want a strong independent north – if Jon

00:03:34.310 --> 00:03:39.570
hands the north to a foreign queen, they’re
not gonna support him . Jon and Tyrion argue

00:03:39.570 --> 00:03:44.270
that the titles and crowns don’t matter
– the white walker apocalypse is coming,

00:03:44.270 --> 00:03:49.270
and they need Daenerys to survive . Tyrion
says that Cersei’s army is coming to help

00:03:49.270 --> 00:03:53.720
as well, but the northerners hate the Lannisters
cause they just fought a war against them.

00:03:53.720 --> 00:03:58.470
And Sansa points out there’s not enough
food for everyone – not much point surviving

00:03:58.470 --> 00:04:01.170
the zombies if everybody starves.

00:04:01.170 --> 00:04:07.040
So at Winterfell, the forces of ice and fire
and Lannisters are coming together, and they

00:04:07.040 --> 00:04:11.110
don’t get along – but they need each other
to survive.

00:04:11.110 --> 00:04:12.860
Tyrion and Sansa reunite.

00:04:12.860 --> 00:04:17.460
They were married for a while, until Joffrey
died and Sansa ran off, leaving Tyrion to

00:04:17.460 --> 00:04:19.560
be accused of Joffrey’s murder.

00:04:19.560 --> 00:04:23.900
Sansa apologises for leaving him hanging – but
they’ve both survived.

00:04:23.900 --> 00:04:28.460
Sansa thinks Tyrion’s an idiot for believing
that Cersei would help them – cause of course,

00:04:28.460 --> 00:04:32.920
Cersei is actually planning to betray everyone
– she tricked Tyrion.

00:04:32.920 --> 00:04:37.470
Tyrion used to have all the best strategies
– but he’s made a lot of bad mistakes

00:04:37.470 --> 00:04:38.470
lately.

00:04:38.470 --> 00:04:41.280
In Season 6, his peace deal in Meereen failed.

00:04:41.280 --> 00:04:43.750
In Season 7, his war plans failed.

00:04:43.750 --> 00:04:46.960
And now his supposed alliance with Cersei
will fail.

00:04:46.960 --> 00:04:51.270
Tyrion's identity and self-worth are built
on his smart political plays.

00:04:51.270 --> 00:04:54.180
So if he continues to fail, who is he?

00:04:54.180 --> 00:04:59.140
Arya and Jon finally reunite, after seven
seasons apart.

00:04:59.140 --> 00:05:03.800
They were close growing up, because they were
both misfits at Winterfell – Jon as a bastard,

00:05:03.800 --> 00:05:05.560
and Arya as a tomboy.

00:05:05.560 --> 00:05:10.910
Jon gave Arya her sword, Needle, and he asks
if she’s used it, but she avoids the question

00:05:10.910 --> 00:05:14.590
– she’s doesn’t like to talk about the
traumatic stuff she’s been through.

00:05:14.590 --> 00:05:18.820
Though Jon mentions that he was killed then
resurrected – which you’d really think

00:05:18.820 --> 00:05:21.260
people would talk about more often.

00:05:21.260 --> 00:05:26.260
Jon tries to badmouth Sansa – he and Arya
used to gang up on their perfect sister when

00:05:26.260 --> 00:05:27.260
they were young.

00:05:27.260 --> 00:05:31.930
But Arya and Sansa bonded last season, and
Arya stands up for her sister.

00:05:31.930 --> 00:05:36.909
Cause “the lone wolf dies, but the pack
survives” – the Starks have to stick together

00:05:36.909 --> 00:05:42.410
. Which is gonna get tricky for Jon – he’s
about to find out that he’s half Stark,

00:05:42.410 --> 00:05:47.330
half Targaryen – will he still be a part
of the Stark pack?

00:05:47.330 --> 00:05:52.350
Davos suggests that Daenerys and Jon should
get married , which would make a lot of sense.

00:05:52.350 --> 00:05:54.230
It could help the northmen accept Daenerys.

00:05:54.230 --> 00:05:57.449
It would unite Jon and Dany’s claims to
the Throne.

00:05:57.449 --> 00:06:00.320
And conveniently enough, Jon and Dany are
in love.

00:06:00.320 --> 00:06:05.860
But Varys gives an ominous warning – he
says that “Nothing lasts” .

00:06:05.860 --> 00:06:10.580
Daenerys and Jon go visit the dragons, who
aren’t doing well in the north – these

00:06:10.580 --> 00:06:13.910
are creatures of fire in a land of ice.

00:06:13.910 --> 00:06:18.169
In Game of Thrones history, there was once
a Targaryen queen who flew her dragon to the

00:06:18.169 --> 00:06:19.169
Wall.

00:06:19.169 --> 00:06:24.370
And the dragon refused to fly beyond the Wall,
which disturbed the queen . It’s like there’s

00:06:24.370 --> 00:06:29.110
something in the north that scares dragons
– probably the white walkers.

00:06:29.110 --> 00:06:32.020
Daenerys and Jon have a cute dragon ride.

00:06:32.020 --> 00:06:37.650
Jon rides the dragon Rhaegal, who’s named
after his real father, Rhaegar – Daenerys’

00:06:37.650 --> 00:06:38.650
brother.

00:06:38.650 --> 00:06:42.770
In the lore, only Targaryens have the special
blood to ride dragons – so the fact that

00:06:42.770 --> 00:06:48.150
Jon can ride should tip Dany off to Jon’s
real identity.

00:06:48.150 --> 00:06:52.840
Dany and Jon make out by a waterfall, which
is a callback to Jon and Ygritte making love

00:06:52.840 --> 00:06:54.690
in a cave with a waterfall.

00:06:54.690 --> 00:07:00.080
Ygritte said she wanted to stay in the cave
forever , and now Dany says she and Jon “could

00:07:00.080 --> 00:07:06.070
stay a thousand years”, but as Varys said,
“Nothing lasts” . Jon and Dany’s love

00:07:06.070 --> 00:07:11.639
seems star-crossed – doomed to end in tragedy,
just like Jon and Ygritte.

00:07:11.639 --> 00:07:16.180
There are theories about Jon becoming a new
Night King, doomed to protect the realm as

00:07:16.180 --> 00:07:18.740
a white walker person forever.

00:07:18.740 --> 00:07:23.760
And Daenerys once had vision of leaving the
Throne, and being with her dead love Drogo.

00:07:23.760 --> 00:07:30.610
So Jon and Dany probably won’t last – they
might get a different kind of forever.

00:07:30.610 --> 00:07:36.330
At Winterfell, Gendry makes weapons of dragonglass,
or obsidian – a volcanic rock that can kill

00:07:36.330 --> 00:07:37.680
white walkers.

00:07:37.680 --> 00:07:43.020
Gendry gives the Hound a sweet dragonglass
axe, and the Hound reunites with Arya.

00:07:43.020 --> 00:07:46.380
Last time they saw each other, Arya left the
Hound for dead.

00:07:46.380 --> 00:07:50.240
They get pretty aggressive with each other
– which is just their way of showing their

00:07:50.240 --> 00:07:51.389
love.

00:07:51.389 --> 00:07:55.600
Arya reunites with Gendry, and he calls her
“my lady”, calling back to his teasing

00:07:55.600 --> 00:07:57.270
in Season 2.

00:07:57.270 --> 00:08:01.680
In the books, it’s said that “Arya has
the hands of a blacksmith” , and some fans

00:08:01.680 --> 00:08:06.650
wonder if Arya might have Gendry’s hand
in marriage – Arya could become Gendry’s

00:08:06.650 --> 00:08:07.650
“lady”.

00:08:07.650 --> 00:08:13.120
But Arya is not lady-like – she asks Gendry
to make her a weapon , which looks like a

00:08:13.120 --> 00:08:16.699
detachable staff with dragonglass at each
end.

00:08:16.699 --> 00:08:21.080
We saw her using this weapon in the trailer
– the Faceless Men trained her to fight

00:08:21.080 --> 00:08:22.740
with staffs.

00:08:22.740 --> 00:08:27.890
Sansa tells Jon that a northern lord, Robett
Glover, is refusing to help the Starks, because

00:08:27.890 --> 00:08:33.540
Jon gave up his crown . So this proves Sansa’s
point – Jon’s submission to Dany has made

00:08:33.540 --> 00:08:35.860
their family less powerful.

00:08:35.860 --> 00:08:40.520
Of course, Jon is also right that Daenerys’
dragons are needed to stop the white walkers.

00:08:40.520 --> 00:08:45.820
But Sansa points out that Jon’s relationship
with Dany is not purely political.

00:08:45.820 --> 00:08:50.680
He loves her, and that could be a problem,
cause as Aemon once said, “Love is the death

00:08:50.680 --> 00:08:55.050
of duty” – Jon might find it difficult
to do things that are good for the realm,

00:08:55.050 --> 00:09:00.320
but not good for Daenerys – like if, say,
Jon has to sacrifice Daenerys to save the

00:09:00.320 --> 00:09:01.320
world.

00:09:01.320 --> 00:09:05.990
Jon and Dany’s arcs are all about balancing
their loves and loyalties against big political

00:09:05.990 --> 00:09:07.940
and magical forces.

00:09:07.940 --> 00:09:12.050
In the endgame, will they choose love or duty?

00:09:12.050 --> 00:09:14.300
Daenerys and Jorah visit Sam.

00:09:14.300 --> 00:09:18.080
Daenerys thanks him for curing Jorah’s embarrassing
skin disease last season.

00:09:18.080 --> 00:09:22.620
But then Sam finds out that Daenerys killed
Sam’s father and brother, because they wouldn’t

00:09:22.620 --> 00:09:23.620
submit to her.

00:09:23.620 --> 00:09:27.310
Sam’s dad was a cunt, but Sam loved his
brother.

00:09:27.310 --> 00:09:31.080
So Sam is filled with grief and anger at Daenerys.

00:09:31.080 --> 00:09:36.290
And Bran chooses that moment to get Sam to
tell Jon the big secret of his parentage.

00:09:36.290 --> 00:09:41.920
Jon’s down in the crypts, by the statue
of Ned Stark – the man who Jon thinks is

00:09:41.920 --> 00:09:42.920
his father.

00:09:42.920 --> 00:09:44.930
But Sam tells him the truth.

00:09:44.930 --> 00:09:48.000
Jon is the son of Ned’s sister, Lyanna.

00:09:48.000 --> 00:09:52.560
And Jon’s father is Rhaegar Targaryen, Daenerys’
eldest brother.

00:09:52.560 --> 00:09:57.649
Jon’s real name is Aegon Targaryen, and
he’s the rightful King of Westeros , ahead

00:09:57.649 --> 00:09:58.970
of Daenerys.

00:09:58.970 --> 00:10:02.279
So this changes a lot for Jon personally.

00:10:02.279 --> 00:10:04.830
Turns out Jon was never a bastard.

00:10:04.830 --> 00:10:07.200
The man who raised him isn’t his father.

00:10:07.200 --> 00:10:10.870
And his girlfriend Daenerys is actually his
aunt.

00:10:10.870 --> 00:10:12.670
Sam pushes the political angle.

00:10:12.670 --> 00:10:17.500
He says that by law, Jon is King of Westeros,
and Daenerys shouldn’t be queen . Could

00:10:17.500 --> 00:10:22.270
this start a rivalry between Jon and Daenerys,
fighting for the Throne?

00:10:22.270 --> 00:10:27.620
Jon doesn’t want be King of Westeros – but
it wouldn’t be the first time he’s reluctantly

00:10:27.620 --> 00:10:29.080
accepted power.

00:10:29.080 --> 00:10:32.040
Sam asks if Daenerys would ever give up her
crown.

00:10:32.040 --> 00:10:36.060
Would she sacrifice the Throne that she’s
been fighting for all this time?

00:10:36.060 --> 00:10:41.520
The answer is probably yes – we saw that
vision in Season 2 of Daenerys turning away

00:10:41.520 --> 00:10:47.740
from the Throne – Jon and Daenerys may sacrifice
what they desire most.

00:10:47.740 --> 00:10:53.070
Jaime Lannister arrives at Winterfell, looking
a lot less blonde than on his last visit.

00:10:53.070 --> 00:10:55.000
And Jaime sees Bran.

00:10:55.000 --> 00:10:58.990
Last time they met, Jaime pushed Bran from
a tower – crippling him and beginning his

00:10:58.990 --> 00:11:02.060
journey to become a psychic tree-wizard.

00:11:02.060 --> 00:11:04.720
How will Bran react to Jaime?

00:11:04.720 --> 00:11:08.740
Maybe he’ll be distant and indifferent like
was seeing Jon again.

00:11:08.740 --> 00:11:09.840
But maybe not.

00:11:09.840 --> 00:11:13.900
Cause after Bran’s fall, he didn’t remember
Jaime pushing him.

00:11:13.900 --> 00:11:18.710
In the books, the three-eyed raven specifically
deletes that memory from Bran’s head.

00:11:18.710 --> 00:11:24.820
Maybe seeing Jaime again will remind Bran
of his fall, and of the boy he used to be.

00:11:24.820 --> 00:11:26.839
This also is a danger to Jaime.

00:11:26.839 --> 00:11:31.279
If the Starks find out that Jaime crippled
Bran – as well as killing Daenerys’ father

00:11:31.279 --> 00:11:36.100
– Jaime might get a warmer welcome to Winterfell
than he’d like.

00:11:36.100 --> 00:11:44.240
So this is more tension and drama to distract
from the real war between the living and the

00:11:44.240 --> 00:11:45.240
dead.

00:11:45.240 --> 00:11:47.390
Down in King’s Landing, Cersei learns that
the Wall has fallen – now, there’s nothing

00:11:47.390 --> 00:11:50.110
between Westeros and the white walkers.

00:11:50.110 --> 00:11:55.100
And Cersei is happy about this . She figures
that the walkers will kill Daenerys and Jon,

00:11:55.100 --> 00:12:00.670
so it’ll be easier for her to hold the Throne
– Cersei is so psychopathic that she welcomes

00:12:00.670 --> 00:12:02.710
the zombie apocalypse.

00:12:02.710 --> 00:12:07.960
To help her hold power, Euron Greyjoy brings
her Harry Strickland, and his mercenary army,

00:12:07.960 --> 00:12:09.120
the Golden Company.

00:12:09.120 --> 00:12:12.530
Cersei is mad that the Company didn’t bring
war elephants.

00:12:12.530 --> 00:12:17.040
It’s weird that the show even mentions the
elephants if we’re not gonna see any – maybe

00:12:17.040 --> 00:12:20.560
the effects budget ran out and they’re just
making a joke of it.

00:12:20.560 --> 00:12:22.470
Or maybe the elephants will come later.

00:12:22.470 --> 00:12:27.930
The Golden Company has a complex history in
the lore which is probably not relevant to

00:12:27.930 --> 00:12:33.720
the show, but the Company has famously never
broken a contract . So maybe, for the first

00:12:33.720 --> 00:12:38.470
time, the Company will break contract, and
betray Cersei – maybe she’ll end up on

00:12:38.470 --> 00:12:40.150
the wrong end of an elephant.

00:12:40.150 --> 00:12:45.680
Cersei has sex with Euron – he asks it as
a condition of their alliance, but she might

00:12:45.680 --> 00:12:51.029
have some actual attraction to his arrogance
and recklessness – Euron’s kinda like

00:12:51.029 --> 00:12:56.019
Jaime was before he got all honourable, and
Cersei tends to choose lovers who remind her

00:12:56.019 --> 00:12:57.310
of her brother.

00:12:57.310 --> 00:13:02.180
Cersei cheats on Jaime with several men in
the books , but Jaime has only ever slept

00:13:02.180 --> 00:13:03.460
with her.

00:13:03.460 --> 00:13:08.380
Euron says that he’ll get Cersei pregnant
, and she has an emotional reaction.

00:13:08.380 --> 00:13:12.100
Supposedly, Cersei is already pregnant with
Jaime’s child.

00:13:12.100 --> 00:13:16.250
That’s why she didn’t drink wine last
season, and how she convinced Tyrion she’d

00:13:16.250 --> 00:13:17.480
help the north.

00:13:17.480 --> 00:13:21.500
But now she is drinking wine, and she’s
upset at the mention of pregnancy.

00:13:21.500 --> 00:13:24.560
So maybe Cersei has lost her child by miscarriage.

00:13:24.560 --> 00:13:29.290
Or maybe she is still pregnant, and she’s
gonna claim that Jaime’s child is Euron’s.

00:13:29.290 --> 00:13:30.940
Or maybe she was never pregnant.

00:13:30.940 --> 00:13:35.510
Cersei once said that a woman’s weapon is
between her legs – she uses sex and her

00:13:35.510 --> 00:13:38.200
body to manipulate people.

00:13:38.200 --> 00:13:40.760
Bronn enjoys the company of some prostitutes.

00:13:40.760 --> 00:13:43.820
He brags about having shot a dragon last season.

00:13:43.820 --> 00:13:46.890
And the women talk about soldiers they know
who’ve been hurt.

00:13:46.890 --> 00:13:52.170
They mention a ginger named Eddie, which is
a reference to Ed Sheeran’s cameo last season.

00:13:52.170 --> 00:13:57.680
Apparently, Dany’s dragon burned his eyelids
off . And Eddie was a nice guy – Arya made

00:13:57.680 --> 00:13:58.900
friends with him.

00:13:58.900 --> 00:14:03.710
So this is a reminder of the human cost of
this war – it’s hurting good innocent

00:14:03.710 --> 00:14:06.180
people and English singer-songwriters.

00:14:06.180 --> 00:14:08.180
Bronn is interrupted by Qyburn.

00:14:08.180 --> 00:14:13.300
He says that Cersei will pay Bronn lots of
gold to kill Jaime and Tyrion – using the

00:14:13.300 --> 00:14:16.540
crossbow that Tyrion used to kill their father
Tywin.

00:14:16.540 --> 00:14:21.820
Cersei has wanted Tyrion dead for years, but
this is the first time she’s moved against

00:14:21.820 --> 00:14:22.820
Jaime.

00:14:22.820 --> 00:14:28.220
Jaime is her twin, he’s all she’s got
left . Wanting him dead shows how far gone

00:14:28.220 --> 00:14:29.660
Cersei is.

00:14:29.660 --> 00:14:34.089
Maybe the reason Cersei was emotional earlier
was because she’s ordered the death of the

00:14:34.089 --> 00:14:36.880
father of her unborn child.

00:14:36.880 --> 00:14:39.050
So what will Bronn do?

00:14:39.050 --> 00:14:43.560
Bronn always said he’s just in it for himself,
and he’ll kill anyone for the right price

00:14:43.560 --> 00:14:49.110
. But Bronn has been through a lot with Tyrion
and Jaime – will he kill his friends , just

00:14:49.110 --> 00:14:50.880
cause the queen told him to?

00:14:50.880 --> 00:14:55.340
It’s like Varys’ riddle in Season 2 – who
really holds power?

00:14:55.340 --> 00:14:58.530
The man with the sword, or the queen with
the crown?

00:14:58.530 --> 00:15:02.440
Maybe Bronn will discover that the real power
is friendship .

00:15:02.440 --> 00:15:05.790
Yara Greyjoy is a prisoner of her uncle Euron.

00:15:05.790 --> 00:15:09.050
And Euron’s a good host compared to the
books.

00:15:09.050 --> 00:15:13.300
In a sample chapter for the upcoming book,
Euron imprisons his brother Aeron.

00:15:13.300 --> 00:15:19.100
He chains him naked to a wall, and drugs him
so he has feverish nightmares of apocalypse.

00:15:19.100 --> 00:15:24.510
He mocks Aeron’s god , and torments him
over childhood sex abuse . He hangs mutilated

00:15:24.510 --> 00:15:29.680
priests from the walls, including a crazed
warlock with his legs cut off . He gets a

00:15:29.680 --> 00:15:34.350
woman pregnant, then rips out her tongue,
and ties her and Aeron to the front of his

00:15:34.350 --> 00:15:40.500
ship, as part of a mass blood sacrifice to
make Euron into an eldritch god – so, yeah

00:15:40.500 --> 00:15:47.140
the Game of Thrones books are gnarly, and
Euron in the show is a Disney pirate in comparison.

00:15:47.140 --> 00:15:52.390
While Euron is rooting the queen, his nephew
Theon boards his ship and kills the crew – including

00:15:52.390 --> 00:15:54.459
Mac from It’s Always Sunny.

00:15:54.459 --> 00:15:59.060
Euron’s ship is called the Silence, cause
he’s removed the tongues of his crew.

00:15:59.060 --> 00:16:02.480
As it turns out, mutes don’t make very good
guards.

00:16:02.480 --> 00:16:07.860
Theon rescues his sister Yara, and she headbutts
him, as payback for leaving her with Euron

00:16:07.860 --> 00:16:09.410
in the first place.

00:16:09.410 --> 00:16:14.889
Yara had once tried to rescue Theon from Ramsay
– now Theon has returned the favour.

00:16:14.889 --> 00:16:19.740
Yara heads home to the Iron Islands, while
Theon heads to help the Starks . Theon had

00:16:19.740 --> 00:16:25.300
once betrayed the Starks, so now he’s trying
to make amends, to redeem his crimes and failures

00:16:25.300 --> 00:16:26.420
one by one.

00:16:26.420 --> 00:16:32.510
He’s still a traumatised broken man, but
“What is dead may never die” , and Theon

00:16:32.510 --> 00:16:35.339
can still do some good.

00:16:35.339 --> 00:16:39.210
Far in the north, Last Hearth is the closest
castle to the Wall.

00:16:39.210 --> 00:16:44.140
This is the home of young Ned Umber – Sansa
sent him up there to bring his people to safety.

00:16:44.140 --> 00:16:49.220
But he was too late – the white walkers
came and killed everyone – raising the dead

00:16:49.220 --> 00:16:52.240
as wights and marching them south.

00:16:52.240 --> 00:16:57.440
Remember that white walkers are the ice demons,
and wights are the zombies – they’re different.

00:16:57.440 --> 00:17:00.290
Beric Edd and Tormund meet at Last Hearth.

00:17:00.290 --> 00:17:05.370
The Night’s Watch and wildlings were enemies
for thousands of years – but now they’re

00:17:05.370 --> 00:17:07.000
allies and friends.

00:17:07.000 --> 00:17:12.360
They find the walkers have left a “message”
– Ned Umber is pinned to a wall in a spiral

00:17:12.360 --> 00:17:13.760
of corpses.

00:17:13.760 --> 00:17:17.140
Ned comes back as a wight, so Beric burns
him.

00:17:17.140 --> 00:17:19.750
The walkers have made corpse-spirals before.

00:17:19.750 --> 00:17:24.470
Cause the spiral was a symbol of the children
of the forest – the children created the

00:17:24.470 --> 00:17:29.150
Night King, the first white walker, at a tree
with this spiral shape.

00:17:29.150 --> 00:17:34.810
So now the Night King is recreating this spiral
as a sort of blasphemy against his creators.

00:17:34.810 --> 00:17:39.970
That’s what the writer of this episode said,
anyway . So it seems like the Night King is

00:17:39.970 --> 00:17:43.290
angry at his creators, like Frankenstein’s
monster.

00:17:43.290 --> 00:17:45.880
He never asked to be made into an ice demon.

00:17:45.880 --> 00:17:50.360
So now he wants to punish the world for making
him what he is.

00:17:50.360 --> 00:17:52.890
This spiral represents his hate.

00:17:52.890 --> 00:17:59.110
And the burning spiral could represent the
fiery magic sacrifice needed to defeat him.

00:17:59.110 --> 00:18:03.860
So in Episode 1, the white walkers are marching
their army of the dead towards Winterfell.

00:18:03.860 --> 00:18:09.460
But the living are still divided, in drama
between Starks Targaryens and Lannisters.

00:18:09.460 --> 00:18:13.240
The situation looks grim, but there is hope.

00:18:13.240 --> 00:18:17.960
When Jon learns his true parentage in the
crypts, this might fulfil a prophecy.

00:18:17.960 --> 00:18:23.280
Melisandre believes that the prince that was
promised, or Azor Ahai, will defeat the white

00:18:23.280 --> 00:18:24.280
walkers.

00:18:24.280 --> 00:18:29.049
And the prophecy in the books goes deeper
– here’s a clip from the audiobook – “When

00:18:29.049 --> 00:18:36.460
the red star bleeds and the darkness gathers,
Azor Ahai shall be born again amidst smoke

00:18:36.460 --> 00:18:43.900
and salt to wake dragons out of stone” . Azor
Ahai will wake dragons from stone.

00:18:43.900 --> 00:18:48.100
One interpretation of this is when Daenerys
hatches dragon eggs that were thought to be

00:18:48.100 --> 00:18:50.550
petrified, turned to stone.

00:18:50.550 --> 00:18:55.880
But another interpretation is that after Jon
learns his Targaryen parentage, in the stone

00:18:55.880 --> 00:19:01.590
crypts, he’ll become a metaphorical dragon
– a fiery Targaryen king.

00:19:01.590 --> 00:19:06.240
Jon has also been born again, and the red
star connects to the red comet.

00:19:06.240 --> 00:19:11.900
So there are a heaps of cool details like
this in the Game of Thrones books – prophecies,

00:19:11.900 --> 00:19:15.580
mysteries, whole plotlines and characters
that aren’t in the tv show.

00:19:15.580 --> 00:19:20.671
And it’s easy to listen to Thrones on audiobook
while you’re in the car, or the train, or

00:19:20.671 --> 00:19:21.990
on dragonback.

00:19:21.990 --> 00:19:27.020
